    docs(readme): document DUCKBRAIN_CONFIG_PATH substrate isolation (AUG-090)
    
    DUCKBRAIN_DATA_DIR + DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACES_PATH alone do not isolate a
    second substrate on a shared host: the namespace registry is the shared
    surface, so /api/namespaces still lists the co-located production
    namespaces and scratch writes can look like production writes. The
    Substrate pin section now shows the full escape hatch — a scratch config
    file with its own namespaceMappings via DUCKBRAIN_CONFIG_PATH (env-only,
    same convention as DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACES_PATH) — and the post-boot
    isolation check. The known-gaps bullet now names the registry as the
    shared surface and points to that section.
    
    Addresses AUG-090
    
